Project Zenith Summary:

1. Introduction & Kickoff: Project Zenith was introduced as a new initiative for data analytics (Alex) and cloud storage optimization (Marcus Cole). Kickoff dates mentioned include June 15th and July 15th, 2023. Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole were identified as leads.

2. Budget: Initial phase one budget was $500,000. It was later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses (Jordan). Finally, the executive board approved a total budget of $2M covering all phases (Budget Approval email).

3. Progress & Findings: Initial findings suggested a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms (Tom). Phase two achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics (Neil). The project is described as surpassing expectations and being a game-changer.

4. Team & Partnerships: The team expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing) (Rebecca). A strategic partnership with TechInnovate, an AI research leader, was secured (Fiona).

5. Security & Meetings: Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Various meetings were scheduled for updates, including August 5th, August 1st, and November 20th."
